### Adding Your Second Rule — MSI Installer Blocking

Click **+ Add** again for a second row:

**Name:**
```
AppLocker - Block Private Browsers MSI
```

**OMA-URI:**
```
./Vendor/MSFT/AppLocker/ApplicationLaunchRestrictions/PrivateBrowserBlock/MSI/Policy
```

**Data Type:**
```
String (XML)
<AppLockerPolicy Version="1">
  <RuleCollection Type="Msi" EnforcementMode="Enabled">

    <!-- Allow MSIs signed by Microsoft -->
    <FilePublisherRule
      Id="b7af5cd8-1111-2222-3333-000000000001"
      Name="Allow - Microsoft Signed MSI"
      Description="Allow Microsoft installer packages"
      UserOrGroupSid="S-1-1-0"
      Action="Allow">
      <Conditions>
        <FilePublisherCondition
          PublisherName="O=MICROSOFT CORPORATION, L=REDMOND, S=WASHINGTON, C=US"
          ProductName="*"
          BinaryName="*">
          <BinaryVersionRange LowSection="*" HighSection="*" />
        </FilePublisherCondition>
      </Conditions>
    </FilePublisherRule>

    <!-- BLOCK: LibreWolf MSI installer -->
    <FilePublisherRule
      Id="b7af5cd8-2222-2222-3333-000000000002"
      Name="BLOCK - LibreWolf Installer"
      Description="Prevents LibreWolf from being installed"
      UserOrGroupSid="S-1-1-0"
      Action="Deny">
      <Conditions>
        <FilePublisherCondition
          PublisherName="*LIBREWOLF*"
          ProductName="*"
          BinaryName="*">
          <BinaryVersionRange LowSection="*" HighSection="*" />
        </FilePublisherCondition>
      </Conditions>
    </FilePublisherRule>

    <!-- BLOCK: Mullvad MSI installer -->
    <FilePublisherRule
      Id="b7af5cd8-3333-2222-3333-000000000003"
      Name="BLOCK - Mullvad Installer"
      Description="Prevents Mullvad Browser from being installed"
      UserOrGroupSid="S-1-1-0"
      Action="Deny">
      <Conditions>
        <FilePublisherCondition
          PublisherName="*MULLVAD*"
          ProductName="*"
          BinaryName="*">
          <BinaryVersionRange LowSection="*" HighSection="*" />
        </FilePublisherCondition>
      </Conditions>
    </FilePublisherRule>

  </RuleCollection>
</AppLockerPolicy>
```

Click **Save**, then click **Next**.

---

## Step 6: Assign the Policy to Devices

1. On the **Assignments** tab you'll see two sections: **Included Groups** and **Excluded Groups**

2. Under **Included Groups**, click **+ Add Groups**

3. Search for and select your target group:
   - For testing: select a **small pilot group** (e.g., `IT-Test-Devices`)
   - For full rollout: select **All Devices** or your main device group

4. Click **Select**, then click **Next**

> ⚠️ **Always test on a small group first** before assigning to all devices

---

## Step 7: Review and Create

1. On the **Review + Create** tab, look over your settings
2. Confirm:
   - Profile name is correct
   - OMA-URI entries are present (you should see 2 rows)
   - Assignment targets the right group
3. Click **Create**

You'll see a success notification. The policy now exists and will push to devices on their next Intune sync.

---

## Step 8: Force the Policy to Apply (On a Test Device)

Intune syncs automatically but can take up to 8 hours. To force it immediately:

### Option A — Via Windows Settings (Easiest)
```
Settings → Accounts → Access Work or School
→ Click your work account → Click "Info"
→ Scroll down → Click "Sync"
```

### Option B — Via Company Portal App
```
Open Company Portal → Click the three dots (···) menu
→ Click "Check Status" or "Sync"